# oracle: kspace_style ewald/disp 1e-5 with a Coulomb-only pair (lj/cut/coul/long: no ewald_order, so the Coulomb term alone) and kspace_modify slab 3.0 (EW3DC correction of the z dipole), boundary p p f, a rocksalt slab of 64 ions, NVE 30 steps.
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 1.2e-14, atoms 8.6e-15.
units           metal
atom_style      charge
boundary        p p f
lattice         fcc 5.64
region          box block 0 2 0 2 -1 3
create_box      2 box
region          slab block 0 2 0 2 0 1.5
create_atoms    1 region slab
lattice         fcc 5.64 origin 0.5 0.0 0.0
create_atoms    2 region slab
mass            1 22.99
mass            2 35.45
set             type 1 charge 1.0
set             type 2 charge -1.0
velocity        all create 300.0 87287 dist gaussian
pair_style      lj/cut/coul/long 7.0
pair_coeff      1 1 0.0100 2.35
pair_coeff      2 2 0.0050 4.40
pair_coeff      1 2 0.0070 3.00
kspace_style    ewald/disp 1.0e-5
kspace_modify   slab 3.0
timestep        0.001
fix             1 all nve
thermo_style    custom step temp pe ecoul elong press pxx pyy pzz
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          10
run             30
